  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the presence of a sure outcome (100% probability), but the individual considers the probability of winning something (non-zero outcome), which is different. The individual does not mention or reflect on whether any outcome is certain (i.e., 100% likely), which is the core of the decision reason. Moreover, since both lotteries lack a sure outcome, the decision reason would be indifferent, but the individual clearly favors B based on higher chance of non-zero gain. The information considered (chance of non-zero win) and the justification (higher probability of winning something) do not align with the decision reason’s focus (presence of a sure outcome). Therefore, there is no evidence the individual used this reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
